questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where a high-throughput Spring Boot service experiences partial database updates and intermittent data corruption during batch operations. The team implemented the following service:

java
@Service
public class TransactionalBatchProcessor {
    private boolean activeBatch = false;

    @Transactional
    public void processBatch(List<String> batchIds) {
        this.activeBatch = true;
        batchIds.parallelStream().forEach(this::processRecord);
        this.activeBatch = false;
    }

    @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW)
    public void processRecord(String id) {
        // Audit logging and database mutation
    }
}


Under load, operations in `processRecord` fail to commit in separate autonomous transactions as expected, and concurrent executions corrupt the state of `activeBatch`.
